  "tagline": "PostgreSQL extension that adds openCypher graph queries alongside SQL.",
  "description": "Apache AGE is a PostgreSQL extension that stores property graphs in Postgres tables and lets you query them with openCypher embedded in SQL, so graph and relational data share transactions, backups and tooling. It grew out of Bitnine's AgensGraph and became a top-level Apache project; releases track each Postgres major (1.8.0 for PostgreSQL 18 in 2026), and Azure Database for PostgreSQL offers it as a supported extension. It is the pragmatic option when your data already lives in Postgres and you need moderate graph querying, but deep traversals are slower than in native graph engines.",
